# Quickstroke — slow working stroke, quick return, then reverse
# Original control program. SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
# Copyright (c) 2026 CrispStrobe
# Reset/reload the supplied model to its saved pose before starting.
# Motor A is the only input. Its direct-drive geometric crank angle is -A.
# These are absolute, unwrapped encoder targets with fresh measured feedback.
# Speeds are degrees per second. A target error over 2 degrees holds and stops.
# Three continuous turns each way expose full strokes away from motor ramps.
# Do not insert pauses at the carriage extrema: that changes the time experiment.
# First run: geometric rotation positive; slow inward and fast outward.
# Reverse run: geometric rotation negative; slow outward and fast inward.
# The carriage is passive. Its measured position is independent of the prediction.
# 2 finite native motor-move blocks; 5 initial/completion/settling guards.
DEVICE SPIKE

WHEN flag clicked:
  lab start
  lab stop motor A hold
  wait 0.5 seconds
  IF (abs of (0 - (lab motor A angle))) > 2 THEN:
    lab stop motor A hold
    stop all
  lab run motor A for (-1080 - (lab motor A angle)) degrees at 30 degrees per second
  lab stop motor A hold
  IF (abs of (-1080 - (lab motor A angle))) > 2 THEN:
    lab stop motor A hold
    stop all
  wait 1.5 seconds
  IF (abs of (-1080 - (lab motor A angle))) > 2 THEN:
    lab stop motor A hold
    stop all
  lab run motor A for (0 - (lab motor A angle)) degrees at 30 degrees per second
  lab stop motor A hold
  IF (abs of (0 - (lab motor A angle))) > 2 THEN:
    lab stop motor A hold
    stop all
  wait 1.5 seconds
  IF (abs of (0 - (lab motor A angle))) > 2 THEN:
    lab stop motor A hold
    stop all
  lab stop motor A hold
